## 2. Problem Understanding

The objective of this challenge is to resolve noisy business entity records from **Source 2 and Source 3** against a deduplicated canonical reference dataset, **Source 1**.

Each source contains business information such as:

- Business/entity name
- Address
- Country

The records in Source 2 and Source 3 may contain spelling variations, formatting differences, abbreviations, missing information, transliteration differences, and other forms of noise.

The system identifies which Source 2 and Source 3 records correspond to the same canonical business entity represented in Source 1.

The solution operates entirely offline and does not use external business databases, geocoding APIs, web search, or other external entity information.

---

## 3. Solution Overview

The MangoCode solution uses a multi-stage entity-resolution pipeline:

```text
Raw Source Data
      |
      v
Data Loading & Auditing
      |
      v
Multilingual Normalization
      |
      v
Candidate Generation / Blocking
      |
      v
Pairwise Feature Engineering
      |
      v
Machine Learning Classification
      |
      v
XGBoost + LightGBM + CatBoost Ensemble
      |
      v
Confidence Thresholding
      |
      v
Global Consistency Resolution
      |
      v
Final Entity Matches
      |
      v
candidate_pairs.tsv
matching_results.tsv
```

The pipeline first reduces the enormous Source 1 × Source 2/3 search space through candidate blocking. The resulting candidate pairs are then evaluated using deterministic similarity features and a machine-learning ensemble.

